---
export const title = 'Mentions';
export const order = 300;
---

<p>
  Every composer in a discussion offers mentions: the main one and each reply
  and edit composer. Typing a trigger (<code>@</code> by default) fires
  <code>search</code> with <code>{'{ trigger, query }'}</code>, which bubbles to
  the discussion. Answer it by setting <code>suggestions</code> (and
  <code>suggestions-loading</code> while you look) on the discussion; it hands
  them to the composer that asked.
</p>
<p>
  <code>triggers</code> sets the trigger characters of every composer
  (<code>"@#"</code> adds a second one, for tickets, say; <code>""</code> turns
  mentions off). <code>mention-href</code>, such as
  <code>"/users/{'{id}'}"</code>, turns mention chips in comments and activity
  into links. <code>submit</code> and <code>edit</code> carry the mentioned
  people in <code>detail.mentions</code>, ready for notifications.
</p>

<pre><code>discussion.addEventListener('search', async event =&gt; {'{'}
  discussion.suggestionsLoading = true;
  discussion.suggestions = await searchPeople(event.detail.query);
  discussion.suggestionsLoading = false;
{'}'});</code></pre>
